sections.text:
A good formation for Garden of Terror is 1-1-3:
3 Heroes cover the side lane where the allied Bruiser Camp is
or, alternatively, the side lane near the next Objective;
1 Hero covers the middle lane;
1 Hero, the Offlaner, covers
the side lane far away from the next Objective.

A good formation for Garden of Terror is 1-3-1:
1 Hero, preferably ranged, covers the lane where the enemy Siege Camp is;
3 Heroes cover the middle lane;
1 Hero, the Offlaner, covers the other side lane.

As shown in the image below, Garden of Terror has a total of 6 Mercenary Camps:
1 Siege Camp (green icon) on the left side of the top lane;
1 Bruiser Camp (blue icon) on the right side of the top lane;
2 Siege Camps (green icon) in the middle lane;
1 Bruiser Camp (blue icon) on the left side of the bottom lane;
1 Siege Camp (green icon) on the right side of the bottom lane.
Mercenary Camps on Garden of Terror disappear from the battlefield
once the Garden Terrors begin spawning (unless their Mercenaries are in combat)
and reappear only after all Garden Terrors have been killed.

Once you know the second Seed's location, it is possible to predict all other Seed's locations.
bottom-left, top-right, bottom-middle, top-left, bottom-right, top-middle;
bottom-right, top-left, bottom-middle, top-right, bottom-left, top-middle;
bottom-left, top-middle, bottom-right, top-left, bottom-middle, top-right;
bottom-right, top-middle, bottom-left, top-right, bottom-middle, top-left.
